[{"author_association":null,"body":"In this `function_call_output` streaming case, the yielded update inherits `lastRole`/`lastMessageId` from prior events. If `function_call_output` is the first output item (as in the added test), both will still be null, so the `ChatResponseUpdate` carrying `FunctionResultContent` will have `Role == null` and `MessageId == null`. That can cause `ToChatResponseAsync` to split the tool output into a separate `ChatMessage` and diverge from the non-streaming `ToChatMessage` behavior (which attaches `FunctionResultContent` to the assistant message). Consider setting an appropriate role (and, if possible, a stable message identifier) before yielding this update so streaming/non-streaming results remain consistent for consumers.
```suggestion
                        case FunctionCallOutputResponseItem functionCallOutputItem:
                            // Ensure role and message id are set so that function results are associated
                            // with the assistant message, matching non-streaming behavior.
                            if (lastRole is null)
                            {
                                lastRole = Microsoft.Extensions.AI.ChatRole.Assistant;
                            }
                            if (lastMessageId is null)
                            {
                                lastMessageId = functionCallOutputItem.CallId;
                            }
