body:
Fixes a resource-leak bug and a consistency violation in `files/index.ts`, and ensures all AI API sessions are properly destroyed on both success and error paths.

## Changes

- **`files/index.ts`** — `writeUrlToFile()` used `throw new Error(...)` instead of returning an error object, bypassing the catch block and bubbling to callers. Also, when `response.body` is null the previously created `FileSystemWritableFileStream` was left open/locked; it is now aborted before returning:
  ```ts
  // Before
  if (!response.body) return { ok: false, message: "Response body is null" };

  // After
  if (!response.body) {
    await writable.abort();
    return { ok: false, message: "Response body is null" };
  }
  ```

- **`language-detector/index.ts`** — `detector.destroy()` was only called on the success path. Moved into a `try/finally` block to guarantee cleanup even when `detect()` throws.

- **`summarizer/index.ts`** — `session.destroy()` was only called on the success path in both `summarizer` and `summarizerStream`. Both now use `try/finally` to ensure the session is always destroyed after creation, including when the summarize call or streaming loop throws.

- **`translator/index.ts`** — `translatorSession.destroy()` was only called on the success path in both `translator` and `translatorStream`. Both now use `try/finally` to ensure the session is always destroyed after creation, including when the translate call or streaming loop throws.

