body:
## Fix: Add Missing Authorization Header and Type Field in MCP Gateway Converters ✅

### Problem
The MCP gateway configuration converters for Claude and Copilot were only adding the `Authorization` header if it already existed in the gateway output. This caused the converted configurations to be missing the required API key authentication headers.

The issue was reported in the smoke-claude workflow where the converted configuration was lacking the authorization header:
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": { "url": "http://0.0.0.0:8080/mcp/github" },
    "playwright": { "url": "http://0.0.0.0:8080/mcp/playwright" },
    "safeoutputs": { "url": "http://0.0.0.0:8080/mcp/safeoutputs" },
    "serena": { "url": "http://0.0.0.0:8080/mcp/serena" }
  }
}
```

### Solution
- [x] Updated `convert_gateway_config_claude.sh` to always add headers.Authorization
- [x] Updated `convert_gateway_config_copilot.sh` to always add headers.Authorization  
- [x] Updated `convert_gateway_config_claude.sh` to include `"type": "http"` for MCP servers
- [x] Merged main branch and recompiled all workflows
- [x] Manually tested the fix with sample gateway output
- [x] Verified with comprehensive test scripts

### Changes Made
1. Modified `actions/setup/sh/convert_gateway_config_claude.sh`:
   - Changed conditional header setting to always create headers object
   - Ensures all MCP servers have Authorization header with API key
   - Now includes `"type": "http"` for HTTP-based MCP servers

2. Modified `actions/setup/sh/convert_gateway_config_copilot.sh`:
   - Applied same fix for consistency
   - Copilot converter now always adds Authorization header

3. Merged main branch:
   - Integrated latest changes from main including MCP gateway log parsing
   - Recompiled all workflow files

### Test Results
Comprehensive tests confirmed the fix works correctly for both converters:

**Claude Output (Updated):**
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://0.0.0.0:8080/mcp/github",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "test-api-key-12345" }
    },
    "playwright": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://0.0.0.0:8080/mcp/playwright",
      "headers": { "Authorization": "test-api-key-12345" }
    },
    ...
  }
}
```

**Copilot Output:**
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "github": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://0.0.0.0:8080/mcp/github",
      "tools": ["*"],
      "headers": { "Authorization": "test-copilot-key-67890" }
    },
    ...
  }
}
```

All MCP servers now include the required Authorization header with the API key and proper type specification. ✅

<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->



<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->



<details>

<summary>Original prompt</summary>

> Reference: https://github.com/githubnext/gh-aw/actions/runs/20873799031/job/59979995478#step:25:1
> 
> The converted configuration is lacking the authorization header with the generated api key.
> 
> This is the config passed to claude:
> 
> {
>   "mcpServers": {
>     "github": {
>       "url": "http://0.0.0.0:8080/mcp/github"
>     },
>     "playwright": {
>       "url": "http://0.0.0.0:8080/mcp/playwright"
>     },
>     "safeoutputs": {
>       "url": "http://0.0.0.0:8080/mcp/safeoutputs"
>     },
>     "serena": {
>       "url": "http://0.0.0.0:8080/mcp/serena"
>     }
>   }
> }


</details>



<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->
---

💡 You can make Copilot smarter by setting up custom instructions, customizing its development environment and configuring Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers. Learn more [Copilot coding agent tips](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-tips) in the docs.

