body:
The `create_project_status_update` handler was failing with NOT_FOUND errors when the direct `projectV2(number)` GraphQL query returned null or failed, even though the project was accessible via the projects list API. This commonly occurs with org projects that require specific token scopes.

## Changes

- **Added fallback mechanism**: When direct project lookup fails, fall back to listing all accessible projects and searching by number
- **Added helper functions**: `listAccessibleProjectsV2()`, `summarizeProjectsV2()`, and `summarizeEmptyProjectsV2List()` for project resolution and error reporting
- **Improved error messages**: Now shows which projects are accessible when lookup fails

## Behavior

**Before:**
```javascript
async function resolveProjectV2(projectInfo, projectNumberInt) {
  const project = await github.graphql(query, { ... });
  if (project) return project;
  throw error;  // Fails immediately
}
```

**After:**
```javascript
async function resolveProjectV2(projectInfo, projectNumberInt) {
  try {
    const project = await github.graphql(query, { ... });
    if (project) return project;
    core.warning(`Direct query returned null; falling back to list search`);
  } catch (error) {
    core.warning(`Direct query failed; falling back to list search`);
  }

  // Fall back to listing all projects
  const list = await listAccessibleProjectsV2(projectInfo);
  const found = list.nodes.find(p => p.number === projectNumberInt);
  if (found) return found;

  throw new Error(`Project not found. Accessible: ${summarizeProjectsV2(list.nodes)}`);
}
```

This matches the existing pattern in `update_project.cjs` which already implements this fallback successfully.

<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->



<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->



<details>

<summary>Original prompt</summary>

> Fix issue in `create_project_status_update`:
> Processing message 16/16: create_project_status_update
> Creating status update for project: https://github.com/orgs/githubnext/projects/73
> Warning: Direct projectV2(number) query failed: Request failed due to following response errors:
>  - Could not resolve to a ProjectV2 with the number 73.
> Error: Failed to create project status update: Request failed due to following response errors:
>  - Could not resolve to a ProjectV2 with the number 73.
> GraphQL Error during: Creating project status update
> Message: Request failed due to following response errors:
>  - Could not resolve to a ProjectV2 with the number 73.
> Errors array (1 error(s)):
>   [1] Could not resolve to a ProjectV2 with the number 73.
>       Type: NOT_FOUND
>       Path: ["organization","projectV2"]
>       Locations: [{"line":3,"column":13}]
> Request: {
>   "query": "query($login: String!, $number: Int!) {\n          organization(login: $login) {\n            projectV2(number: $number) {\n              id\n              number\n              title\n              url\n            }\n          }\n        }",
>   "variables": {
>     "login": "githubnext",
>     "number": 73
>   }
> }
> Response data: {
>   "organization": {
>     "projectV2": null
>   }
> }
> ✓ Message 16 (create_project_status_update) completed successfully


</details>



