[{"author_association":null,"body":"The subtest name/message says it verifies the *detection_agentic_execution step* uses AWF, but the assertion only checks that the overall detection job contains the substring "sudo -E awf". This can pass even if the AWF call is moved to a different step. Consider extracting just the step block (starting at "id: detection_agentic_execution" and ending at the next step entry) and asserting "sudo -E awf" within that block.
```suggestion
				// Narrow the check to the detection_agentic_execution step block.
				stepID := "id: detection_agentic_execution"
				startIdx := strings.Index(detectionJob, stepID)
				require.NotEqual(t, -1, startIdx, "detection job must contain %q", stepID)

				// Start the block at the step ID occurrence.
				agenticStepSection := detectionJob[startIdx:]

				// Heuristically end the block at the start of the next step ("- " at the beginning of a line).
