The current implementation would return `ConnectionProfile.WiFi` for a WiFi+VPN connection (since WiFi is checked first at line 334), which may not accurately represent that the connection is going through a VPN. Consider documenting this behavior or checking for VPN first if VPN status is important to users:

```csharp
// Check VPN first, as it may overlay other transports
if (capabilities.HasTransport(TransportType.Vpn))
{
    // VPN is active - could report VPN or check underlying transport
    // For now, classify as Unknown since VPN overlays other connections
    return ConnectionProfile.Unknown;
}

// Check underlying transport types
if (capabilities.HasTransport(TransportType.Wifi))
{
    return ConnectionProfile.WiFi;
}
// ... rest of checks
```

Alternatively, if the underlying transport is more important than the VPN overlay, the current order is acceptable but should be documented.","body_updated_after_merge":false,"commit_id":"6d1ecb474d976cdf6eb979f927e57b8d6891b0fd","created_at":"2025-11-27T09:41:28Z","diff_hunk":"@@ -253,50 +283,84 @@ public IEnumerable<ConnectionProfile> ConnectionProfiles
