I have to agree, the current code feels too "messy". Some alternatives that came to mind:
- Move `CheckValue` out of `MakeQueryInvocation`, make it responsibility of a caller and adjust the problematic caller to call `CheckValue` only once.
- Remove conditional logic around  `CheckValue` call from `MakeQueryInvocation`. Always call it unconditionally. At the same time adjust `CheckValue` to not mutate the node, but `Update` the node and return a new instance under DEBUG. After these changes, it will be possible to pass the original node to `CheckValue` multiple times.

