body:
The `sortTemplates` function had a critical bug where `getPriority` used outer scope variables (`a.name`, `b.name`) in its fallback case, causing both `getPriority(a.id)` and `getPriority(b.id)` to return identical values for non-priority templates. This made alphabetical sorting non-functional.

**Changes:**
- Refactored `getPriority` to return only fixed priority values (1-4)
- Moved alphabetical comparison outside `getPriority` as fallback when priorities match
- Fixed duplicate regex pattern: second httptrigger condition now correctly matches decorated variants without leading word boundary

**Before:**
```typescript
function getPriority(id: string): number {
    if (/\bhttptrigger\b/i.test(id)) return 1;
    else if (/\bhttptrigger/i.test(id)) return 2;  // Never reached - same pattern
    else if (/\btimertrigger\b/i.test(id)) return 3;
    else return a.name.localeCompare(b.name) === -1 ? 4 : 5;  // Uses outer scope
}
return getPriority(a.id) - getPriority(b.id);  // Always 0 for non-priority templates
```

**After:**
```typescript
function getPriority(id: string): number {
    if (/\bhttptrigger\b/i.test(id)) return 1;
    else if (/httptrigger/i.test(id)) return 2;  // Now catches decorated variants
    else if (/\btimertrigger\b/i.test(id)) return 3;
    else return 4;
}

const priorityDiff = getPriority(a.id) - getPriority(b.id);
if (priorityDiff !== 0) return priorityDiff;
return a.name.localeCompare(b.name);  // Alphabetical fallback
```

