[{"author_association":null,"body":"SwipeView mixes Auto Layout constraints with manual Frame manipulation, which can cause Auto Layout conflicts. The _contentView is pinned to the parent with constraints (lines 221-227), but ShowSwipeItems, ResetPosition, and HandlePan directly set _contentView.Frame (lines 86, 181, 193). When a view has TranslatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints = false and active constraints, directly setting Frame will cause Auto Layout warnings and unpredictable behavior. Consider either: (1) using constraint animations for swipe gestures by deactivating/reactivating constraints with updated constants, or (2) setting TranslatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints = true for _contentView and avoiding Auto Layout constraints entirely for the swipe animation wrapper.
```suggestion
			_contentView.TranslatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints = true;
			_contentView.AddSubview(newContent);
			newContent.UpdateAlign();
			NativeView.AddSubview(_contentView);
```","body_updated_after_merge":false,"commit_id":"b8e571b6e8e057ad6c9218ab59b985b173f53750","created_at":"2026-02-20T18:16:53Z","diff_hunk":"@@ -211,14 +211,20 @@ partial void OnContentChanged(View? oldContent, View? newContent)
