body:
`import DEME` crashes immediately with `filesystem error: status: Bad address []` because `JitHelper::CACHE_DIR`'s static initializer calls `std::filesystem::exists(DEMERuntimeDataHelper::data_path)` before `data_path` is constructed — a classic static init order fiasco. In the Python `.so`, `core` is linked before `DEMERuntimeDataHelper_python`, so `JitHelper.cpp`'s initializers fire while `data_path` is still zero-initialized. Passing its uninitialized internal pointer to `stat()` returns `EFAULT`, which `std::filesystem` rethrows as a fatal exception.

## Changes

- **`JitHelper.cpp`**: Remove `JitHelper::resolveCacheDir()` from the static initializer for `CACHE_DIR`; default-initialize to an empty path instead.
- **`JitHelper.cpp`**: Lazily resolve `CACHE_DIR` on first call to `buildProgram()` using `std::call_once`, by which point `SetPathPrefix()` has already run and `data_path` is valid.
- **`.gitignore`**: Expanded to a comprehensive CUDA-C++ gitignore covering build directories, CMake artifacts, compiled binaries, CUDA-specific outputs (`.cubin`, `.fatbin`, `.ptx`, `.sass`, `.cuobj`), Python packaging artifacts, IDE configs, and `_codeql_detected_source_root`.
- **`_codeql_detected_source_root`**: Deleted the stale CodeQL symlink from the repository.

```cpp
// Before — crashes if data_path not yet constructed
std::filesystem::path JitHelper::CACHE_DIR = JitHelper::resolveCacheDir();

// After — safe empty default; resolved lazily on first use
std::filesystem::path JitHelper::CACHE_DIR;

// In buildProgram():
static std::once_flag cache_dir_init_flag;
std::call_once(cache_dir_init_flag, []() { CACHE_DIR = resolveCacheDir(); });
```

Non-Python builds are unaffected: `resolveCacheDir()` still runs before any kernel compilation, and `data_path` is always valid by that point via shared-library init ordering.

