I have thought about this some more and at this point I think it's the superior approach. There are definitely some negatives, like all initial coroutine calls requiring an extra call, but we trade that for all resume calls requiring one less call. We also avoid the whole `is` business, which was my original gripe, and we fix the dynamic dispatch issue. And something else that occurred to me is that I think we also no longer need the awkward default value stuff because the only call to our actual function is now always a normal one.

