> @copilot I have cleaned up a few things and reverted some changes. Your recent commits caused a bit of a mess because you had some internal error, so please ignore any instructions you still have queu...

Fixed in commit db6806f.

For `super.X()` calls inside non-static `ClassField` coroutines: before building the state machine, the compiler now scans for `TField(TConst TSuper, FInstance(supercls, params, cf))` patterns and for each unique super method access:

1. Adds a `_hx_super_X_0` helper method to the original class (where `super` is syntactically valid) that simply forwards all args to `super.X(args)`
2. Replaces the `super.X` access with `_gthis._hx_super_X_0` — a regular instance method call through the captured `_gthis` reference

Generated JS for the example:
```js
// Helper on Child class (super is valid here):
_hx_super_test_0: function(_hx_continuation) {
    return Parent.prototype.test.call(this, _hx_continuation);
}

// Inside the thunk (closure) — no super, just a normal call through _gthis:
var _hx_tmp = _gthis._hx_super_test_0(_hx_continuation.completion);
```

