> @copilot I have pushed a commit where the idea is to accurately track during the initial transformation if our current coroutine captures any outside variables or accesses `this` or `super`. I'm prett...

Fixed in commit 84219f3.

Two issues were preventing the LocalFunc inline path from working:

1. **`captured` field not cleared**: `ContinuationClassBuilder.create` always sets `captured = Some cf` for `LocalFunc` (needed for the thunk ctor). When `inline_state_machine = true` the ctor must not take a `captured` arg, so `coro_class.captured` is now `mutable` and is set to `None` before building the class.

2. **Own args counted as outer captures**: `expr_to_coro` didn't know about the function's own `tf_args`, so any reference to them triggered `has_capture_vars = true`. Added an `args` parameter and pre-declare them in `vars` at the start.

With both fixes, `not ctx.captures_this && not ctx.has_capture_vars` now correctly identifies LocalFuncs that can use the inline path. All hxcoro JS tests pass (`ALL TESTS OK`).","body_updated_after_merge":null,"commit_id":null,"created_at":"2026-02-21T22:39:43Z","diff_hunk":null,"duplicate_id_conflict":false,"event_at":"2026-02-21T22:39:43+00:00","event_key":"pr_comment:3939624186","event_type":"pr_comment","html_url":null,"id":"3939624186","in_reply_to_id":null,"is_feedback_candidate":false,"is_human":false,"line":null,"original_commit_id":null,"original_line":null,"original_position":null,"original_start_line":null,"path":null,"position":null,"pull_request_review_id":null,"pull_request_url":null,"side":null,"source_table":"pr_comments","source_url":"https://github.com/haxefoundation/haxe/pull/12645","start_line":null,"start_side":null,"state":null,"submitted_at":null,"temporal_relation":"during_pr","updated_at":null,"url":null,"user":"Copilot","user_id":"198982749","user_type":"Bot"},{"author_association":null,"body":"@copilot I have refactored the `captured` situation in https://github.com/HaxeFoundation/haxe/pull/12645/changes/da4d691438b5fc99337663d9463a9d80ffe5458b because I didn't like that mutable state. Instead of it being a record, we now pass it around to the places that need it. Its presence also governs our generation mode (inline in `invokeResume` vs. thunk-call). Please check if my change had any unintended side-effects.

