> @copilot I have cleaned up a bit and moved the deferred expansion to where I think it should be, which is `handle_locals`.
> 
> Unfortunately, we must have broken something quite basic because this no l...

Fixed in commit 821b462.

**Root cause**: `add_expr` in `coroFromTexpr.ml` uses `has_side_effect` to decide whether to add an expression to the CFG block. In the original code, `make_inline_return` produced a real side-effectful `TBlock`. With the deferred mechanism introduced in commit a03cdb8, it produces a `TLocal` placeholder instead — and `TIf(x, TLocal_placeholder, None)` evaluates to side-effect-free, so `add_expr` silently dropped the if-statement.

**Fix**: Added a `contains_deferred` helper alongside `has_side_effect` in `add_expr`. Any expression containing a deferred-expansion placeholder is kept even if it looks side-effect-free.

All hxcoro JS tests pass (`ALL TESTS OK`).","body_updated_after_merge":null,"commit_id":null,"created_at":"2026-02-22T10:10:50Z","diff_hunk":null,"duplicate_id_conflict":false,"event_at":"2026-02-22T10:10:50+00:00","event_key":"pr_comment:3940637003","event_type":"pr_comment","html_url":null,"id":"3940637003","in_reply_to_id":null,"is_feedback_candidate":false,"is_human":false,"line":null,"original_commit_id":null,"original_line":null,"original_position":null,"original_start_line":null,"path":null,"position":null,"pull_request_review_id":null,"pull_request_url":null,"side":null,"source_table":"pr_comments","source_url":"https://github.com/haxefoundation/haxe/pull/12645","start_line":null,"start_side":null,"state":null,"submitted_at":null,"temporal_relation":"during_pr","updated_at":null,"url":null,"user":"Copilot","user_id":"198982749","user_type":"Bot"},{"author_association":null,"body":"@copilot I have cleaned up a bit and merged parts of this into `development` already, so the diff is much smaller now. Things seem to be generally working alright.

One thing I'd still like to address is the type parameter situation. At the moment we're relying on `inside_to_outside` and `subst_eloop` to get this right, but in my estimation it shouldn't be wrong in the first place.

I think what we should do is lock our generation mode to either the thunking or the invokeResume inlining right after the `expr_to_coro` call. At that point we have all the necessary information: we know how many states there are and whether or not there are any captures. With this knowledge it should be possible to create `vcontinuation` and all related locals and expressions with the correct types.

