+    context += "```yaml\nsafe-outputs:\n  create-pull-request:\n    allow-manifest-files: true\n```\n";
+  }","duplicate_id_conflict":false,"event_at":"2026-03-07T15:09:29+00:00","event_key":"inline_comment:2899868321","event_type":"inline_comment","html_url":null,"id":"2899868321","in_reply_to_id":null,"is_feedback_candidate":false,"is_human":false,"line":null,"original_commit_id":"dbcc31ec83c6ddb10e0e3053978f751248f546cf","original_line":null,"original_position":73,"original_start_line":null,"path":"actions/setup/js/handle_agent_failure.cjs","position":86,"pull_request_review_id":"3908920332","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/pulls/19958","side":null,"source_table":"pr_review_comments","source_url":"https://github.com/github/gh-aw/pull/19958","start_line":null,"start_side":null,"state":null,"submitted_at":null,"temporal_relation":"during_pr","updated_at":"2026-03-07T15:09:29Z","url":null,"user":"Copilot","user_id":null,"user_type":"Bot"},{"author_association":null,"body":"@copilot I would like a third option "fallback-as-issue". When this option is present create_pull_request  should follow the existing issue creation fallback path (which includes a PR creation intent link) when manifest files are being modified. A clear explanation for _why_ the fallback path is being taken should be included in the issue text along with instructions that the user should review the code carefully before creating a PR. 

Also this whole option should also be present on "push-to-pull-request-branch" which should also have the fallback issue path and/or hard failure depending on the option chosen. 

Also AGENTS.md and all files under .github should be included in the "manifest files". ","body_updated_after_merge":false,"commit_id":"ae482bf76a084ff0a3113b899423ff435fb0ac43","created_at":"2026-03-07T15:13:37Z","diff_hunk":"@@ -5263,6 +5263,11 @@
                 "github-token-for-extra-empty-commit": {
                   "type": "string",
                   "description": "Token used to push an empty commit after PR creation to trigger CI events. Works around the GITHUB_TOKEN limitation where pushes don't trigger workflow runs. Defaults to the magic secret GH_AW_CI_TRIGGER_TOKEN if set in the repository. Use a secret expression (e.g. '${{ secrets.CI_TOKEN }}') for a custom token, or 'app' for GitHub App auth."
+                },
+                "allow-manifest-files": {","duplicate_id_conflict":false,"event_at":"2026-03-07T15:13:37+00:00","event_key":"inline_comment:2899873053","event_type":"inline_comment","html_url":null,"id":"2899873053","in_reply_to_id":null,"is_feedback_candidate":true,"is_human":true,"line":null,"original_commit_id":"dbcc31ec83c6ddb10e0e3053978f751248f546cf","original_line":null,"original_position":5,"original_start_line":null,"path":"pkg/parser/schemas/main_workflow_schema.json","position":1,"pull_request_review_id":"3908926718","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/pulls/19958","side":null,"source_table":"pr_review_comments","source_url":"https://github.com/github/gh-aw/pull/19958","start_line":null,"start_side":null,"state":null,"submitted_at":null,"temporal_relation":"during_pr","updated_at":"2026-03-07T15:13:37Z","url":null,"user":"dsyme","user_id":null,"user_type":"User"},{"author_association":null,"body":"Done in 6114b60. Three changes implemented:

1. **`"fallback-as-issue"` option**: Both `create-pull-request` and `push-to-pull-request-branch` now accept `allow-manifest-files: "fallback-as-issue"`.
   - For `create-pull-request`: the branch is pushed normally, then a review issue is created with a PR creation intent URL, a `> [!WARNING]` banner explaining the protection triggered, and a "review carefully before creating the PR" instruction.
   - For `push-to-pull-request-branch`: instead of pushing, a review issue is created with the target PR link, patch download/apply instructions, and the same review warning. Issue creation is deferred until after PR metadata (repoParts, prTitle, pullNumber) is resolved so the issue can include a direct link to the target PR.

2. **`AGENTS.md` added to manifest files**: `getAllManifestFiles()` now appends `AGENTS.md` as a hardcoded extra entry (matched by basename anywhere in the repo).

3. **`.github/` path-prefix protection**: New `getProtectedPathPrefixes()` in Go returns `[".github/"]`. A new `checkForProtectedPaths(patchContent, prefixes)` JS helper (backed by `extractPathsFromPatch`) checks full paths rather than basenames — so any file under `.github/` (workflows, CODEOWNERS, Dependabot config, etc.) is protected. Both prefixes are injected as `protected_path_prefixes` in handler configs.

Schema updated to `oneOf: [boolean, enum["fallback-as-issue"]]` for both safe output types. Docs updated with a three-option table and coverage of `AGENTS.md`/`.github/`.","body_updated_after_merge":false,"commit_id":"ae482bf76a084ff0a3113b899423ff435fb0ac43","created_at":"2026-03-07T15:53:09Z","diff_hunk":"@@ -5263,6 +5263,11 @@
