eligible_feedback_json:
[{"actor": "Naptie", "body": "@copilot
1. Although the email_update_required_for_binding is displayed, no actual email update is taking place. Please make sure to update their email (I don't know how exactly you can hook in to do this, I'm guessing you can either hook into the binding process directly to update their email address, or manually obtain their remote profile using their access_token and the respective settings from the adapter to get to know the remote email address in the session callback of lib/auth/index.server.ts).

2. The WeChat bind success alert dismissed very shortly after I navigated to the page. It's because of the removal of the wechatToken param. Please try to fix this.", "body_updated_after_merge": null, "date_basis": "created_at", "event_at": "2026-01-20T22:23:58Z", "event_key": "pr_comments:3835137685:d25a1bb86e143c9bbcbc9ce8540e683537e0e53d5d9726ff6532b51d0d5c1be1:1", "parent_review_event_key": null, "request_at": "2026-01-20T20:08:47Z", "request_event_key": "pr_timeline:3835137685:ab828859462322880d581928401b19793e836114097705f6303a4cdf0b83fbca:1", "review_state": null, "role_proxy": "non_author_user", "source_event_at": "2026-01-20T22:23:58Z", "source_table": "pr_comments", "source_url": "https://github.com/Naptie/nearcade/pull/66#issuecomment-3775233272"}, {"actor": "Naptie", "body": "@copilot
1. I've added automatic WeChat token refresh and a function `sendWeChatTemplateMessage` to easily send template messages. Now, you're responsible for sending the template message with ID (that can be found from the environment variable 'WECHAT_TEMPLATE_QUEUE_NOTIFICATION') and payload (`machine`: the new property `machineName` in queue position, `slot`: the slot index, `status`: a text message, explaining the current status (e.g. it's your turn now, or how many ahead, or someone else joined/left your positon)). To send this message, we should add new properties that our physical device sitting in the claimed shop is required to provide by POSTing to /api/shops/[source]/[id]/queues: in QueuePosition, add `machineName` string and `isPrivate` boolean. Then, I will explain in what circumstances should you send this template message:
a) if a card (a QueueMember) is newly inserted or removed by physical operation so that it was not present/is no longer present across all queues within this shop, DO NOT send message;
b) if the belonging position of a card (a QueueMember) switches state from `queued` to `playing`, SEND to inform that it's their turn now, or if the state switches BETWEEN `queued` AND `deferred`, SEND to inform about status update, or if the state switches FROM `playing` TO ANY OTHER STATE, DO NOT send message;
c) if the belonging position of a card progresses within the same queue, SEND to inform about progression;
d) if the belonging position of a card moves to another queue, SEND to inform about queue switching;
e) if the belonging position of a card has its members list updated, SEND to inform about their new playmates;
Since none of the cases requires persistency, you can simply do a before-and-after check as new queues get reported. But this will require the endpoint to switch from per-game style to report-them-all style, i.e. requires a thorough data upload of queues across different games in the entire shop, just make sure to update the expected POST request body accordingly.

2. In the frontend, for a claimed shop, the total number of attendance and per-game (accumulated) attendance are not updated according to data from queues. Make sure those stats (in the sidebar) get updated by queues data.", "body_updated_after_merge": null, "date_basis": "created_at", "event_at": "2026-01-21T11:47:46Z", "event_key": "pr_comments:3835137685:b686d31606b542634805ab6bcac6f2c5d67076470e3d5e5dcf6555f0bffe00d3:1", "parent_review_event_key": null, "request_at": "2026-01-20T20:08:47Z", "request_event_key": "pr_timeline:3835137685:ab828859462322880d581928401b19793e836114097705f6303a4cdf0b83fbca:1", "review_state": null, "role_proxy": "non_author_user", "source_event_at": "2026-01-21T11:47:46Z", "source_table": "pr_comments", "source_url": "https://github.com/Naptie/nearcade/pull/66#issuecomment-3777666710"}, {"actor": "Naptie", "body": "@copilot 
I've updated queue position to use `isPublic` instead so as to align with my client-side app. Now, please add a lock icon (wrapped in a purple triangle (filleted corner)) as a private indicator to the top right corner of a position in the frontend. And for a single position, we use a vivid background color and a border to indicate status & privacy setting (playing, public queued, private queued, deferred), instead of a badge separately. For position display, use a single indicator only, and use daisyUI tooltip to display the status text.", "body_updated_after_merge": null, "date_basis": "created_at", "event_at": "2026-01-21T14:50:04Z", "event_key": "pr_comments:3835137685:9b117f396a3980c66b242d3742f2742015978f19d961bf6766804ac86449d4e1:1", "parent_review_event_key": null, "request_at": "2026-01-20T20:08:47Z", "request_event_key": "pr_timeline:3835137685:ab828859462322880d581928401b19793e836114097705f6303a4cdf0b83fbca:1", "review_state": null, "role_proxy": "non_author_user", "source_event_at": "2026-01-21T14:50:04Z", "source_table": "pr_comments", "source_url": "https://github.com/Naptie/nearcade/pull/66#issuecomment-3778534222"}, {"actor": "Naptie", "body": null, "body_updated_after_merge": null, "date_basis": "submitted_at", "event_at": "2026-01-21T16:06:47Z", "event_key": "pr_reviews:3835137685:eb3a9c6245aa5bbb7d2b12485d8aacbb114109f81db76b3bc9fec552bac27857:1", "parent_review_event_key": null, "request_at": "2026-01-20T20:08:47Z", "request_event_key": "pr_timeline:3835137685:ab828859462322880d581928401b19793e836114097705f6303a4cdf0b83fbca:1", "review_state": "APPROVED", "role_proxy": "non_author_user", "source_event_at": "2026-01-21T16:06:47Z", "source_table": "pr_reviews", "source_url": "https://github.com/Naptie/nearcade/pull/66#pullrequestreview-3688067705"}]

