🔴 **Integration test guard removed, causing Docker-dependent tests to run unconditionally**

The `describe.runIf(process.env.CI || process.env.INTEGRATION)` guard was removed from the LocalStack integration tests in `AwsSsmSecretProvider.test.ts`, replacing it with a plain `describe(...)`. This means the integration tests—which start a LocalStack Docker container—will now always run during `pnpm test` or `pnpm test:ci`. On developer machines or CI environments without Docker available, these tests will fail with container startup errors, breaking the test suite.

```suggestion
describe.runIf(process.env.CI || process.env.INTEGRATION)('AwsSsmSecretProvider (integration with LocalStack)', () => {
```

