🟡 **Azure integration test leaks `AZURE_POD_IDENTITY_AUTHORITY_HOST` environment variable**

In `beforeAll`, `process.env.AZURE_POD_IDENTITY_AUTHORITY_HOST` is set at `tests/envilder/infrastructure/azure/AzureKeyVaultSecretProvider.test.ts:197`, but `afterAll` (lines 209-218) only saves and restores `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED` — it never cleans up `AZURE_POD_IDENTITY_AUTHORITY_HOST`. This env var will leak into subsequent test suites running in the same process, potentially causing `DefaultAzureCredential` in other tests to point at a dead Lowkey Vault endpoint after the container is stopped.

```suggestion
  afterAll(async () => {
    if (container) {
      await container.stop();
    }
    if (originalTlsRejectUnauthorized === undefined) {
      delete process.env.NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED;
    } else {
      process.env.NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED = originalTlsRejectUnauthorized;
    }
    delete process.env.AZURE_POD_IDENTITY_AUTHORITY_HOST;
  });
```

