🔴 **GitHub Action `provider` default always overrides `$config.provider` from map file**

The `provider` input in `action.yml` has `default: "aws"` (line 19). Because GitHub Actions always resolves `${{ inputs.provider }}` to the default value when the user doesn't set it, `INPUT_PROVIDER` is always `"aws"`. In `Gha.ts:33`, `provider || undefined` evaluates to `"aws"` (truthy), and at `Gha.ts:57`, `...(provider && { provider })` always spreads `{ provider: "aws" }`, unconditionally overriding `fileConfig.provider` from `$config` in the map file.

This means users who follow the documentation and set `$config.provider: "azure"` in their map file will have it silently ignored — the GHA will always attempt to use AWS. The E2E test (`e2e/gha.test.ts:300`) doesn't catch this because it calls `node dist/index.js` directly without setting `INPUT_PROVIDER`, so `$config` works in tests but fails in real GitHub Actions workflows.

The fix is to remove `default: "aws"` from `action.yml`, since the application code already defaults to `"aws"` in `ContainerConfiguration.ts:48`: `config.provider?.toLowerCase() || 'aws'`.

```suggestion
    required: false
```

