🟡 **Retry logic for push operations only handles AWS throttling errors, not Azure**

The `retryWithBackoff` method in `PushEnvToSecretsCommandHandler` was updated to say it "Handles throttling errors from cloud providers" (line 163), but the `isThrottlingError` check at lines 179-185 only matches AWS-specific error names (`TooManyUpdates`, `ThrottlingException`, `TooManyRequestsException`). Azure Key Vault throttling errors throw `RestError` with `statusCode: 429` — the `error.name` is `'RestError'`, which doesn't match any of the checked names. As a result, when pushing secrets to Azure Key Vault under throttling conditions, the operation will fail immediately without retrying, even though retries would succeed. The Azure provider at `src/envilder/infrastructure/azure/AzureKeyVaultSecretProvider.ts:28-29` already uses `statusCode`-based checks for 404, so the pattern for Azure status-code errors is established in this PR.

*(Refers to lines 179-185)*

