body:
When `wrap-non-model-return` is enabled, LRO operations whose final result is a non-model type (e.g. `string`) were returned unwrapped — inconsistent with the HLC behavior and non-LRO operations which already wrap correctly.

## Root cause
`checkWrapNonModelReturn` explicitly excluded all LRO operations via an early return, so the wrapping logic never ran for them.

## Changes

- **`checkWrapNonModelReturn`**: Removed blanket LRO exclusion. Added an LRO-specific branch that checks `lroMetadata.finalResponse.result` (the TCGC final result type — `SdkModelType | SdkArrayType | SdkBuiltInType`) against the same no-wrap criteria: model → skip, model array → skip, `unknown` with `treatUnknownAsRecord` → skip, otherwise wrap.

- **`buildDeserializeFunction`**: In the LRO-only branch, when `shouldWrap` is true, resolves the wrapper type alias (`GetIkeSasResponse`) as the deserializer return type. Changed the `shouldWrap` return-value path to use `deserializedRoot` instead of the hard-coded `"result.body"` to correctly handle LRO sub-path segments.

- **`getLroOnlyOperationFunction`**: When `shouldWrap` is true, uses `resolveReference(refkey(operation, "response"))` as the effective LRO result type, so the operation signature becomes `PollerLike<OperationState<T>, T>` with the wrapper type.

**Before / After:**
```ts
// Before
export function getIkeSas(...): PollerLike<OperationState<string>, string>
// deserializer: return result.body;

// After
export type GetIkeSasResponse = { body: string };
export function getIkeSas(...): PollerLike<OperationState<GetIkeSasResponse>, GetIkeSasResponse>
// deserializer: return { body: result.body };
```

- **Test**: Added scenario to `wrapNonModelReturn.md` using `ArmResourceActionAsync` with a string scalar final result, covering the model alias, deserializer, and operation return type.

