Adds SwipeView control matching .NET MAUI's SwipeView API for revealing context actions via swipe gestures.

## Components

**Core abstractions:**
- `SwipeView` - Container with `Content` property and directional item collections (`LeftItems`, `RightItems`, `TopItems`, `BottomItems`)
- `SwipeItem` - Action item with text, background color, and invoked callback
- `SwipeItems` - Collection with `Mode` (Reveal/Execute) and `SwipeBehaviorOnInvoked` (Auto/Close/RemainOpen)
- Supporting enums: `SwipeDirection`, `SwipeMode`, `SwipeBehaviorOnInvoked`

**Platform implementations:**
- iOS: `UIPanGestureRecognizer` with UIView animation
- Android: `GestureDetector` with TranslationX animation

## Usage

```csharp
var swipeView = new SwipeView
{
    RightItems = new SwipeItems
    {
        Items = 
        {
            new SwipeItem 
            { 
                Text = "Delete", 
                BackgroundColor = Colors.Red,
                Invoked = item => HandleDelete()
            },
            new SwipeItem 
            { 
                Text = "Archive", 
                BackgroundColor = Colors.Orange,
                Invoked = item => HandleArchive()
            }
        }
    },
    Content = new Label { Text = "Swipe left to see actions" }
};

// Programmatic control
swipeView.Open(SwipeDirection.Left);
swipeView.Close();

// Events
swipeView.SwipeStarted = (view, direction) => { };
swipeView.SwipeChanging = (view, direction, offset) => { };
swipeView.SwipeEnded = (view, direction, isOpen) => { };
```

## Notes

- Horizontal swipes implemented (most common use case)
- Threshold property controls activation distance
- Item widths differ by platform (75 pt iOS, 200 px Android) to account for unit differences
- Follows existing Spice patterns: partial classes, `[ObservableProperty]`, Action-based events

