body:
`gh aw audit` had no visibility into guard policy enforcement decisions (integrity filtering, repo scoping) from the MCP Gateway. These events appear as JSON-RPC error responses with codes -32001 through -32006 in `rpc-messages.jsonl`, per the access control specification.

### Parsing (`gateway_logs.go`)

- Extended `rpcError` with `Data` field to capture guard policy error context (reason, repository, details)
- Added `GuardPolicyEvent` struct and error code constants (-32001 to -32006) matching the MCP Gateway spec
- `parseRPCMessages()` now detects guard policy errors in RESPONSE entries and classifies them by code
- `processGatewayLogEntry()` handles `GUARD_POLICY_BLOCKED` event type from `gateway.jsonl`
- Added `isGuardPolicyErrorCode()` and `guardPolicyReasonFromCode()` helpers
- Guard policy metrics aggregated across runs in `displayAggregatedGatewayMetrics()`

### Audit report (`audit_report.go`, `audit_report_render.go`)

- `GuardPolicySummary` struct with per-category block counts (integrity, repo scope, access denied, blocked user, permissions, private repo) and per-tool/per-server breakdowns
- Integrated into `MCPToolUsageData` via `buildGuardPolicySummary()`
- `renderGuardPolicySummary()` renders block reason breakdown, most-blocked-tools table, and event details
- Server usage table gains a "Guard Blocked" column when events are present

### Example log entry parsed

```json
{"direction":"IN","type":"RESPONSE","server_id":"github","payload":{
  "jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"error":{
    "code":-32006,
    "message":"Content integrity below minimum threshold",
    "data":{"reason":"integrity_below_minimum","details":"Content integrity 'unapproved' is below minimum 'approved'"}
  }
}}
```

### Tests

7 new unit tests covering error code detection, RPC message parsing with/without data field, gateway.jsonl event handling, summary aggregation, and end-to-end extraction.

