When `visible` is true, this effect always calls `setSelectedRecords(derivedRecords)`. Since `derivedRecords` is recomputed from `optionMap`, and `optionMap` is rebuilt every render (because `realOptions` is recreated on each render by `resolveOptions`), the array identity changes even when the contents are the same. That causes the effect to set state on every render, which can lead to a render loop or continuous re-renders while the popup is open. This regression appears after removing the memoized `deriveRecordsFromValue` behavior.

Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.","body_updated_after_merge":true,"commit_id":"48aa558b917c86686dc6aa2627e59129462a7f73","created_at":"2026-02-09T04:55:47Z","diff_hunk":"@@ -108,15 +106,19 @@ export function MobileLazySelect(props: Readonly<LazySelectProps>) {
