The path comparison logic here is a bit complex and contains redundant checks. The `strpos()`/`stripos()` checks with appended directory separators already handle exact matches, making the `===` and `strcasecmp()` checks unnecessary. On Windows, the case-sensitive check is also redundant.

This logic can be simplified for better readability and to remove the redundant operations.

```php
        $is_windows = DIRECTORY_SEPARATOR === '\';
        if ( $is_windows ) {
            if ( 0 === stripos( $path . DIRECTORY_SEPARATOR, $allowed . DIRECTORY_SEPARATOR ) ) {
                return true;
            }
        } elseif ( 0 === strpos( $path . DIRECTORY_SEPARATOR, $allowed . DIRECTORY_SEPARATOR ) ) {
            return true;
        }
